# Open WebUI Credentials Configuration
#
# You can configure credentials in three ways:
#
# 1. Direct environment variables (simplest for static credentials)
# OPENWEBUI_URL=https://owu.mysite.com
# OPENWEBUI_API_KEY=sk-your-api-key-here
#
# 2. Command-based retrieval (for secrets managers like 1Password)
# OPENWEBUI_URL_COMMAND=op item get "OpenWebUI API Key" --fields label=url
# OPENWEBUI_API_KEY_COMMAND=op item get "OpenWebUI API Key" --fields label=password --reveal
#
# 3. Use defaults in the scripts (for development only - not recommended for production)
#
# Priority: Direct env var > Command > Default
#
# Examples for different secret managers:
#
# 1Password:
# OPENWEBUI_URL_COMMAND=op item get "OpenWebUI API Key" --fields label=url --reveal
# OPENWEBUI_API_KEY_COMMAND=op item get "OpenWebUI API Key" --fields label=password --reveal
#
# AWS Secrets Manager:
# OPENWEBUI_URL_COMMAND=aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id openwebui-url --query SecretString --output text
# OPENWEBUI_API_KEY_COMMAND=aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id openwebui-api-key --query SecretString --output text
#
# HashiCorp Vault:
# OPENWEBUI_URL_COMMAND=vault kv get -field=url secret/openwebui
# OPENWEBUI_API_KEY_COMMAND=vault kv get -field=api_key secret/openwebui
#
# pass (Unix password manager):
# OPENWEBUI_URL_COMMAND=pass show openwebui/url
# OPENWEBUI_API_KEY_COMMAND=pass show openwebui/api-key
